django.template.base.VariableDoesNotExist: Failed lookup for key [errors] in [{'True': True, 'False': False, 'None': None}, {'widget': {'name': 'body', 'is_hidden': False, 'required': False, 'value': '<section id="strap-usage" aria-labelledby="strap-usage-title"><p>Proper strap technique lets you relax your grip, transfer power efficiently, and keep a smooth rhythm. Follow the steps below to fit and use your straps.</p><ol><li><strong>Proper Hand Placement</strong><br>Insert your hand <i>from underneath</i> the strap so it lies across the back of your hand. The adjustment buckle should face outward (away from your palm).</li><li><strong>Slide Your Hand In</strong><br>Feed your hand deeper into the strap until it rests across the base of your fingers and the back of your hand. Adjust so it’s snug but not tight.</li><li><strong>Create a Support Loop</strong><br>With your hand in the strap, form a natural loop by letting your thumb rest against the strap on the palm side. This loop helps keep your hand secure and prevents slipping during your swing.</li><li><strong>Maintain a Relaxed Grip</strong><br>Walk with a light, relaxed hold on the handle—avoid clenching. Let the strap carry the load as you push back, then briefly open your hand during the back swing and re-grip as the pole comes forward.</li></ol><h3>Why it matters</h3><p>Straps add support and stability, improving power transfer and reducing hand fatigue. Correct strap use promotes a more natural, efficient technique and a better overall experience.</p><h3>Quick tips</h3><ul><li>Right strap on right hand, left strap on left hand (they’re often labeled “R” and “L”).</li><li>If your fingers tingle or the strap rubs, loosen and re-adjust.</li><li>Keep the buckle flat and off your skin to avoid chafing.</li></ul></section>', 'attrs': {'class': 'django_ckeditor_5', 'id': 'id_body'}, 'template_name': 'django_ckeditor_5/widget.html'}, 'config': {'toolbar': ['heading', 'codeBlock', '|', 'outdent', 'indent', '|', 'bold