django.template.base.VariableDoesNotExist: Failed lookup for key [errors] in [{'True': True, 'False': False, 'None': None}, {'widget': {'name': 'body', 'is_hidden': False, 'required': False, 'value': '<p>Cooling down after Nordic Walking is important to gradually reduce your heart rate, relax your muscles, and prevent stiffness. Here are ten cool-down exercises you can incorporate:</p><ol><li><strong>Slow Walking:</strong> After your walk, gradually slow down your pace. Continue walking at a slower speed for a few minutes to ease your heart rate back to its normal range.</li><li><strong>Hamstring Stretch:</strong> Stand with one foot in front of the other and gently lean forward, keeping your back straight, to stretch your hamstrings.</li><li><strong>Calf Stretch:</strong> Stand facing a wall or tree, place one foot behind you, and press your heel into the ground to stretch your calf muscles.</li><li><strong>Quad Stretch:</strong> Stand on one leg and gently pull your other heel toward your buttocks to stretch your quadriceps.</li><li><strong>Hip Flexor Stretch:</strong> Step one foot behind you, bend your front knee, and gently push your hips forward to stretch your hip flexors.</li><li><strong>Trunk Rotation:</strong> Stand with your feet hip-width apart and slowly twist your torso to one side and then the other to relax your spine.</li><li><strong>Shoulder Rolls:</strong> Roll your shoulders forward and backward to release tension in your shoulders and upper back.</li><li><strong>Neck Stretches:</strong> Gently tilt your head to one side and hold for a few seconds, then switch to the other side to release tension in your neck.</li><li><strong>Deep Breathing:</strong> Take a few minutes to practice deep, calming breaths. Inhale deeply through your nose, hold for a few seconds, and exhale slowly through your mouth.</li><li><strong>Hydration and Nutrition:</strong> Drink water and, if needed, have a light, healthy snack to replenish your energy and support recovery.