django.template.base.VariableDoesNotExist: Failed lookup for key [errors] in [{'True': True, 'False': False, 'None': None}, {'widget': {'name': 'body', 'is_hidden': False, 'required': False, 'value': '<p>While Nordic Walking is a safe and enjoyable activity for most people, there are some potential hazards to be aware of. Understanding these risks can help you stay safe and get the most out of your walks.</p><figure class="image image_resized" style="width:24.33%;"><img style="aspect-ratio:1024/1024;" src="/uploads/HotNordicWalker.png" width="1024" height="1024"></figure><ol><li><strong>Uneven Terrain:</strong> Rough or uneven ground can increase the risk of tripping or stumbling. Stay alert and watch your footing.</li><li><strong>Weather Conditions:</strong> Rain, snow, or ice can make surfaces slippery. Choose appropriate footwear and be cautious in wet or cold conditions.</li><li><strong>Wildlife Encounters:</strong> In certain regions, encounters with wildlife can occur. Stay aware of your surroundings and follow local safety guidelines.</li><li><strong>Overexertion:</strong> Pushing yourself too hard can cause fatigue or injury. Listen to your body and take breaks when needed.</li><li><strong>Improper Equipment:</strong> Ill-fitting poles or unsuitable footwear can lead to discomfort, blisters, or joint strain. Always use properly adjusted poles and supportive shoes.</li><li><strong>Traffic Hazards:</strong> Walking near roads can expose you to vehicle traffic. Stay on sidewalks or designated walking paths whenever possible.</li><li><strong>Dehydration:</strong> Inadequate fluid intake may cause dehydration or heat-related issues. Carry water and stay hydrated throughout your walk.</li><li><strong>Lack of Sun Protection:</strong> Extended exposure to the sun without sunscreen, hats, or sunglasses can result in sunburn or heat exhaustion.</li><li><strong>Medical Conditions:</strong> Individuals with pre-existing health issues should monitor their condition and consult a healthcare provider before engaging in Nordic Walking.</li><li><strong>Tripping Over Poles:</strong> Beginners may occasionally trip on their own poles. Practice proper technique and maintain awareness of pole placement.</li><li><strong>Group Dynamics:</strong> During group walks, coordination and communication are key to avoiding collisions and ensuring a smooth, enjoyable experience.</li></ol><p>By staying mindful of these potential hazards and taking simple precautions — such as wearing proper gear, staying hydrated, and walking at a comfortable pace — you can enjoy the many benefits of Nordic Walking safely and confidently.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', 'attrs': {'class': 'django_ckeditor_5', 'id': 'id_body'}, 'template_name': 'django_ckeditor_5/widget.html'}, 'config': {'toolbar': ['heading', 'codeBlock', '|', 'outdent', 'indent', '|', 'bold', 'italic', 'link', 'underline', 'strikethrough', 'code', 'subscript', 'superscript', 'highlight', '|', 'bulletedList', 'numberedList', 'todoList', '|', 'blockQuote', 'insertImage', '|', 'fontSize', 'fontFamily', 'fontColor', 'fontBackgroundColor', 'mediaEmbed', 'removeFormat', 'insertTable', 'sourceEditing'], 'language': 'en', 'blockToolbar': ['paragraph', 'heading1', 'heading2', 'heading3', '|', 'bulletedList', 'numberedList', '|', 'blockQuote'], 'image': {'toolbar': ['imageTextAlternative', '|', 'imageStyle:alignLeft', 'imageStyle:alignRight', 'imageStyle:alignCenter', 'imageStyle:side', '|', 'toggleImageCaption', '|'], 'styles': ['full', 'side', 'alignLeft', 'alignRight', 'alignCenter']}, 'table': {'contentToolbar': ['tableColumn', 'tableRow', 'mergeTableCells', 'tableProperties', 'tableCellProperties'], 'tableProperties': {'borderColors': [{'color': 'hsl(4, 90%, 58%)', 'label': 'Red'}, {'color': 'hsl(340, 82%, 52%)', 'label': 'Pink'}, {'color': 'hsl(291, 64%, 42%)', 'label': 'Purple'}, {'color': 'hsl(262, 52%, 47%)', 'label': 'Deep Purple'}, {'color': 'hsl(231, 48%, 48%)', 'label': 'Indigo'}, {'color': 'hsl(207, 90%, 54%