django.template.base.VariableDoesNotExist: Failed lookup for key [errors] in [{'True': True, 'False': False, 'None': None}, {'widget': {'name': 'body', 'is_hidden': False, 'required': False, 'value': '<p>Even though Nordic Walking is simple to learn, some common mistakes can limit its benefits or lead to discomfort. Here are the most frequent errors and tips on how to avoid them:</p><ol><li><strong>Incorrect Leg and Arm Coordination:</strong> Moving the same arm and leg together instead of in opposition can disrupt your rhythm and balance.</li><li><strong>Uncoordinated Arm and Leg Movements:</strong> Ensure that your arm swing matches your stride naturally — opposite arm to opposite leg.</li><li><strong>Insufficient Arm Extension:</strong> Bending elbows too much or gripping the handle tightly prevents a full arm swing. Keep your arms relaxed and extend them naturally.</li><li><strong>Planting Poles Too Far Ahead:</strong> Poles should never go past your lead foot. Keep them angled backward for proper propulsion.</li><li><strong>No Arm Swing:</strong> A stiff or minimal arm swing reduces the workout’s effectiveness. Let your arms move freely and rhythmically.</li><li><strong>Tension in Neck and Shoulders:</strong> Holding too tightly or poor posture can create tension. Relax your shoulders and loosen your grip.</li><li><strong>Inability to Walk Faster:</strong> Overly tight or short movements limit your stride. Relax, extend your arms, and push off with purpose.</li><li><strong>Wrist Tension:</strong> Keeping wrists rigid prevents fluid motion. Let them move naturally with the pole swing.</li><li><strong>Head Down:</strong> Looking down constantly strains your neck and reduces balance. Keep your gaze forward and enjoy the scenery.</li><li><strong>Dragging Poles:</strong> Failing to lift poles properly can cause them to catch on the ground. Lift and plant them actively.</li><li><strong>Small Arm Swing and Steps:</strong> Tiny steps and short arm swings limit momentum. Use a full stride and natural arm motion.</li><li><strong>Incomplete Arm Swing:</strong> Not releasing the strap when the pole is behind your body restricts movement. Open your hand at the back of each swing.</li><li><strong>Incorrect Posture:</strong> Leaning too far forward or backward causes imbalance. Maintain a tall, upright position with relaxed shoulders.</li><li><strong>Gripping Handles Too Tightly:</strong> Over-gripping can cause forearm pain. Hold handles loosely, allowing space between your palm and the handle.</li><li><strong>Failure to Engage Core Muscles:</strong> Not activating your core reduces stability and power. Keep your abdominal muscles gently engaged.</li><li><strong>Inadequate Breathing:</strong> Shallow or irregular breathing can lead to fatigue. Practice deep, rhythmic breathing for endurance and relaxation.</li><li><strong>Lack of Posture Awareness:</strong> Forgetting about posture diminishes effectiveness. Stay upright, relaxed, and mindful throughout your walk.</li></ol><p>By being aware of these common mistakes and practicing good technique, you can enjoy smoother, more efficient, and more rewarding Nordic Walking sessions.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>', 'attrs': {'class': 'django_ckeditor_5', 'id': 'id_body'}, 'template_name': 'django_ckeditor_5/widget.html'}, 'config': {'toolbar': ['heading', 'codeBlock', '|', 'outdent', 'indent', '|', 'bold', 'italic', 'link', 'underline', 'strikethrough', 'code', 'subscript', 'superscript', 'highlight', '|', 'bulletedList', 'numberedList', 'todoList', '|', 'blockQuote', 'insertImage', '|', 'fontSize', 'fontFamily', 'fontColor', 'fontBackgroundColor', 'mediaEmbed', 'removeFormat', 'insertTable', 'sourceEditing'], 'language': 'en', 'blockToolbar': ['paragraph', 'heading1', 'heading2', 'heading3', '|', 'bulletedList', 'numberedList', '|', 'blockQuote'], 'image': {'toolbar': ['imageTextAlternative', '|', 'imageStyle:alignLeft', 'imageStyle:alignRight', 'imageStyle:alignCenter', 'imageStyle:side', '|', 'toggleIm