                                                                                                                                  </style><p><strong>Welcome aboard!</strong> Your application to organize a Nordic Walking group has been reviewed and approved. You’ll receive an email with access details and a ready-to-edit first event template for your group.</p><div class="nwu-toc"><p><strong>Quick Menu</strong></p><ol><li><a href="#approval-email">Approval Email</a></li><li><a href="#sign-in">Sign In to the Admin Panel</a></li><li><a href="#change-password">Change Your Password</a></li><li><a href="#admin-menu">Admin Menu &amp; Events</a></li><li><a href="#list-events">List of Events</a></li><li><a href="#edit-template">Edit the First Event Template</a><ol><li><a href="#ckeditor">a) Event Description (CKEditor)</a></li><li><a href="#main-photo">b) Event Main Picture (Banner)</a></li><li><a href="#coords">c) Latitude &amp; Longitude (Google Maps)</a></li><li><a href="#website-ready">d) Mark “Website is ready”</a></li></ol></li><li><a href="#tips">7. Tips &amp; Notes</a></li></ol><div class="nwu-badge">Tip: Click any item to jump to that section</div></div><div class="nwu-card" id="approval-email"><h3>1. Approval Email</h3><p>The NWU admin reviews all applications and may <strong>accept or reject</strong> them.</p><p>When your application is accepted, you will receive an email with the subject line:&nbsp;<br><strong>Subject:</strong> <i>Congratulations on Your Accepted Application to Organize an NWU Group!</i></p><p>The beginning of the email will look similar to this:</p><p><i>Dear Team,&nbsp;</i>&nbsp;<br><i>Your Full Name &lt;your email&gt;</i>&nbsp;<br><i>Congratulations - and welcome aboard!</i></p><h4>Status &amp; Permissions</h4><p>After acceptance, you officially become an <strong>Organizer and Administrator of your group</strong>. You gain access to the <strong>Admin Panel</strong>, where you can manage your group’s events.</p><div class="nwu-backtop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></div></div><div class="nwu-card" id="sign-in"><h3>2. Sign In to the Admin Panel</h3><p>Click the Admin Panel link provided in your Approval email.</p><p>Log in using your <strong>email and password</strong>.</p><ul><li>If you are a new user, your <strong>initial password</strong> will be included in the acceptance email.</li><li>Please read the email carefully.</li></ul><div class="nwu-callout"><strong>Important:</strong> You should change your password after logging in.</div><div class="nwu-imgph">Admin login screen:</div><figure class="image"><img style="aspect-ratio:372/336;" src="/uploads/AdminPanelLogin.jpg" width="372" height="336"></figure><div class="nwu-backtop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></div></div><div class="nwu-card" id="change-password"><h3>3. Change Your Password</h3><p>After logging in:</p><ol><li>Click <strong>Change Password</strong> (top-right corner, between <strong>View Site</strong> and <strong>Log Out</strong>).</li><li>Enter your old password.</li><li>Enter your new password <strong>twice</strong>.</li><li>Click the blue <strong>“Change My Password”</strong> button.</li></ol><div class="nwu-imgph">Change password in Admin Panel. &nbsp;<br>(Click on any below images to enlarge - it will open in a new tab):&nbsp;</div><figure class="image"><a href="/uploads/AdminPanelChangePassword_CgDQfDS.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img style="aspect-ratio:1885/313;cursor:zoom-in;" src="/uploads/AdminPanelChangePassword_CgDQfDS.jpg" alt="Admin Panel – Change Password" width="1885" height="313"></a></figure><figure class="image"><a href="/uploads/AdminPanelChangePassword2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img style="aspect-ratio:1036/435;cursor:zoom-in;" src="/uploads/AdminPanelChangePassword2.jpg" alt="Admin Panel – Change Password (Step 2)" width="1036" height="435"></a></figure><div class="nwu-backtop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></div></div><div class="nwu-card" id="admin-menu"><h3>4. Admin Menu &amp; Events</h3><p>Once you have logged in and changed your password, you will see the <strong>Admin Panel sidebar</strong> with the sections you have access to.</p><p>Now it’s time to create your <strong>first event</strong> for your newly created group! You will see the <strong>CORE</strong> section, which includes the <strong>List of Events</strong>.</p><figure class="image image_resized" style="height:auto;width:100%;"><a href="/uploads/AdminPanelListOfEvents_0LnpEy6.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img style="aspect-ratio:1898/359;cursor:zoom-in;" src="/uploads/AdminPanelListOfEvents_0LnpEy6.jpg" alt="Admin Panel – List of Events" width="1898" height="359"></a></figure><div class="nwu-backtop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></div></div><div class="nwu-card" id="list-events"><h3>5. List of Events</h3><p>Click <strong>List of Events</strong> under the <strong>CORE</strong> section.</p><p>You will see on the right side:</p><ul><li>A <strong>pre-created template</strong> for your first event</li></ul><p>Click on the <strong>event name</strong> to open it for editing.</p><figure class="image"><a href="/uploads/AdminPanelEventTemplate.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img style="aspect-ratio:905/851;cursor:zoom-in;" src="/uploads/AdminPanelEventTemplate.jpg" alt="Admin Panel – Event Template" width="905" height="851"></a></figure><div class="nwu-backtop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></div></div><div class="nwu-card" id="edit-template"><h3>6. Edit the First Event Template</h3><p>To create your first real event, edit the template (for example: <span class="nwu-code">“John’s Sunny Walkers Riga”</span>). You may change <strong>any details</strong> to reflect your actual event.</p><h4>Required Fields</h4><p>Please complete all required fields:</p><ul><li>Event name</li><li>Date</li><li>City</li><li>Country</li><li>Start time</li><li>Duration</li><li>Distance</li><li>Latitude and longitude</li></ul><div class="nwu-note"><strong>Date format:</strong> Use <span class="nwu-code">21 Dec 2025</span> (day–month–year, with the month as a 3-letter abbreviation).</div><h4>Other Fields</h4><ul><li>Event description (rich text editor / CKEditor)</li><li>Event photo (main event image)</li><li>Photo credit</li><li>Photo URL</li></ul><div class="nwu-card" id="ckeditor"><h4>a) Event Description (Text Box/Editor)</h4><p>We strongly recommend adding <strong>detailed information</strong> about your event. You may include:</p><ul><li>Terrain description</li><li>What to bring</li><li>What to expect</li><li>Weather considerations</li><li>Benefits of this walk</li></ul><p>Adding a <strong>photo of the meeting place</strong> helps participants find you more easily.</p><p>The text field supports:</p><ul><li>Headings</li><li>Bold / italic text</li><li>Bullet and numbered lists</li><li>Links</li><li>Images</li></ul><p><strong>Formatting tips:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Headings:</strong> Use the Heading dropdown (e.g., <i>Route</i>, <i>What to Bring</i>).</li><li><strong>Lists:</strong> Great for schedules, gear, or directions.</li><li><strong>Links:</strong> Select text → click the Link icon → paste a URL.</li><li><strong>Images:</strong> Click the image icon → Upload → choose a file. Recommended width: ~700 px.</li></ul></div><div class="nwu-note">Click the link to view detailed Text Editor instructions (opens in a new tab): <a href="https://www.nordicwalkingunited.org/en/tutorials/using-the-text-editor-while-creating-events-and-bl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Using the Text Editor While Creating Events and Blogs&nbsp;</a></div><div class="nwu-card" id="main-photo"><h4>b) Event Main Picture (Banner Image)</h4><p>Under <strong>Event Main Picture</strong>, click <strong>Choose File</strong> to upload the main banner/background image.</p><p>This image:</p><ul><li>Appears on the global events page as a background for your event</li><li>Displays at a predefined size (no resizing needed before upload)</li></ul><p><strong>Image guidelines:</strong></p><ul><li>Use only <strong>Creative Commons</strong> or other <strong>free/open-license</strong> images</li><li>License-protected images are <strong>not allowed</strong></li><li>You are always welcome to use <strong>your own photos</strong></li></ul><p><strong>Recommended subjects:</strong></p><ul><li>Local park or trail</li><li>Walking path</li><li>City landmark</li><li>Nordic walking scene relevant to your group</li></ul><p><strong>Finding images:</strong></p><ol><li>Go to Google Images</li><li>Choose <strong>Usage rights</strong></li><li>Select an appropriate Creative Commons license</li></ol><p><strong>Credits &amp; URLs:</strong></p><ul><li>Enter the author name in <strong>Photo credit</strong></li><li>Paste the original source link in <strong>Photo URL</strong></li></ul></div><div class="nwu-card" id="coords"><h4>c) Latitude &amp; Longitude (Google Maps)</h4><p>Latitude and longitude help participants locate the <strong>exact meeting point</strong>.</p><p><strong>How to get coordinates:</strong></p><ol><li>Open Google Maps.</li><li>Search for your meeting location.</li><li>Right-click (or long-press on mobile) on the exact spot.</li><li>Copy the coordinates shown (example: <span class="nwu-code">56.951865327302016, 24.11872785575965</span>).</li><li>Paste them into the <strong>Latitude and Longitude</strong> field.</li></ol><div class="nwu-note"><strong>Format:</strong> <span class="nwu-code">lat, lon</span> (comma + space)</div><p><strong>Precision tip:</strong> Drop the pin exactly where people meet (parking lot, entrance, trailhead sign).</p><div class="nwu-imgph">Google maps coordinates example:</div><figure class="image"><a href="/uploads/GoogleMaps.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img style="aspect-ratio:1497/907;cursor:zoom-in;" src="/uploads/GoogleMaps.jpg" alt="Google Maps view" width="1497" height="907"></a></figure></div><div class="nwu-card" id="website-ready"><h4>d) Mark “Website is ready”</h4><p>Once all event information is complete:</p><ol><li>Check the box <strong>“Website is ready”</strong></li><li><p>Click <strong>Save</strong></p><figure class="image"><img style="aspect-ratio:473/241;" src="/uploads/AdminPanelWebsiteIsReady_hP7BNkb.jpg" width="473" height="241"></figure></li></ol><p>This publishes your event:</p><ul><li>On the NWU Global Map</li><li>On the Events and Nordic Walking United Group pages</li></ul><p>Your event becomes visible worldwide, and anyone who registers with NWU can join.</p><p>All moderators of your group will be notified when your group is approved and when the first event goes live.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><div class="nwu-imgph">Example of "Website is Ready" Event in Admin portal:</div><figure class="image"><a href="/uploads/AdminPanelEventTemplateFilled2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img style="aspect-ratio:1060/812;cursor:zoom-in;" src="/uploads/AdminPanelEventTemplateFilled2.jpg" alt="Admin Panel – Event Template Filled" width="1060" height="812"></a></figure><div class="nwu-imgph">And, that is how this event will look on the NWU website:</div><figure class="image"><a href="/uploads/EventOnTheWebsite.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img style="aspect-ratio:885/836;cursor:zoom-in;" src="/uploads/EventOnTheWebsite.jpg" alt="Event displayed on the website" width="885" height="836"></a></figure></div><div class="nwu-backtop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></div></div><div class="nwu-card" id="tips"><h3>7. Tips &amp; Notes</h3><ul><li>Your initial password is sent in the acceptance email — please change it after your first login.</li><li>Use clear, friendly, and detailed descriptions so participants know what to expect.</li><li>Upload a high-quality landscape image for the best appearance.</li><li>Include Photo credit and Photo URL when using CC-licensed images.</li><li>Double-check Date, City/Country, and Latitude/Longitude before marking “Website is ready”.</li><li>For help, contact us via <a href="/contact/contact"><strong>Contact Us</strong></a></li></ul><div class="nwu-backtop"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></div></div></div>', "created_at" = '2025-10-15 23:21:20.101545', "updated_at" = '2026-01-19 21:47:30.158825' WHERE "core_nwu_manual"."id" = 5; args=('Step 2. After Your Application Is Approved - Create your First Event', 'application-accepted', 'team', 2, 'Application accepted', '<div class="nwu-tutorial"><style>\r\n                                                                                                                                    .nwu-tutorial{\r\n                                                                                                                              font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, Segoe UI, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif;\r\n                                                                                                                              line-height: 1.85;\r\n                                                                                                                              color: #1f2937;\r\n                                                                                                                              max-width: 920px;\r\n                                                                                                                              margin: 0 auto;\r\n                                                                                                                              font-size: 20px;\r\n                                                                                                                font-weight: 450;\r\n                                                                                                                     \r\n                                                                                                                                    }\r\n                                                                             