ou wish</p><div style="background-color:#fff8cc;border-left:6px solid #f2c94c;margin:18px 0;padding:14px 16px;"><strong>Important:</strong> Images should be no more than <strong>700 × 700 px</strong>. Larger images may take up too much space in the blog section.</div></li><li><p style="margin-left:22px;">Use the editor tools to format your post and make it clear, welcoming, and beautiful</p></li></ul><div class="nwu-note" style="background-color:#fff7cc;border-radius:10px;margin:14px 0;padding:12px 14px;">Click the link to view detailed Text Editor instructions (opens in a new tab): <a href="https://www.nordicwalkingunited.org/en/tutorials/using-the-text-editor-while-creating-events-and-bl/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Using the Text Editor While Creating Events and Blogs&nbsp;</a></div><p style="text-align:right;"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></p><h3 id="step4">Step 4. Publish Your Blog</h3><ol><li>Review your post for clarity and layout.</li><li>Click <strong>Save</strong> or <strong>Publish</strong>.</li><li>Your blog will be visible to the entire NWU community.</li></ol><p style="text-align:right;"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></p><h3 id="step5">Step 5. Manage Comments on Your Blog</h3><ul><li>Read comments from community members.</li><li>Reply to comments to encourage engagement.</li><li>Delete inappropriate comments if needed.</li></ul><p style="text-align:right;"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></p><h3 id="step6">Step 6. Delete Your Blog Post</h3><ol><li>Open the blog post in the Admin Panel.</li><li>Click <strong>Delete</strong>.</li><li>Confirm the deletion.</li></ol><p style="text-align:right;"><a href="#top">↑ Back to menu</a></p><div style="background-color:#f3fff1;border-left:6px solid #27ae60;margin:18px 0;padding:14px 16px;"><strong>NWU reminder:</strong> Blogs help preserve memories, build connection, and inspire others to join Nordic Walking 🌞</div></div>', '2026-01-19 22:14:38.967517', '2026-01-19 22:27:40.855075', 38); alias